  "question": {
    "text": "If the cubic equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has a purely imaginary root, then (where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)",
    "image": null
